    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§101 & 106, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7669\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation to the exemption of certain parcels of land\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo allow a restaurant that has an interest in the manufacture of\ncertain liquor and beer to obtain a liquor license.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 2. Amends Section 106 (13) to allow a restaurant/bar and\nentertainment venue to apply for an on- premises license to serve\nalcohol.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Alcoholic Beverage Control Law prohibits an establishment with an\ninterest, whether direct or indirect, from manufacturing and selling\nproduct at retail. The original intent of the law was to encourage\ncompetition in the post-prohibition era, however, in many\ncircumstances it now discourages economic development and hinders job\nand tax revenue growth.\n\nThis bill will allow a nationally-recognized entertainment venue to\nlocate in the City of Syracuse within the metes and bounds set forth\nin the legislation which describe the location of a large retail\nshopping center. The location of this venue within such shopping\ncenter will be on the third level across from three elevators and\nadjacent to what is known as the \"Canyon\" area of the shopping center\nin a space designated L323 as per lease agreements between the venue\nand the shopping center and as specified on the venue's liquor\nlicense.\n\nThe venue is expected to hire 150 employees and contribute significant\nsales tax revenue.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIncreased tax revenue.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
