    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7669A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation to the exemption of certain parcels of land\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: To allow a restaurant that has an\ninterest in the manufacture of certain liquor and beer to obtain a\nliquor license.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS: Section 1. Amends Section 106 (13) to\nallow a restaurant/bar and entertainment venue to apply for an on-\npremises license to serve alcohol.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: The Alcoholic Beverage Control Law prohibits an\nestablishment with an interest, whether direct or indirect, from\nmanufacturing and selling product at retail. The original intent of\nthe law was to encourage competition in the post-prohibition era,\nhowever, in many circumstances it now discourages economic development\nand hinders job and tax revenue growth.\n\nThis bill will allow a nationally-recognized entertainment venue to\nlocate in the City of Syracuse within the metes and bounds set forth\nin the legislation which describe the location of a large retail\nshopping center. The location of this venue within such shopping\ncenter will be on the third level across from three elevators and\nadjacent to what is known as the \"Canyon\" area of the shopping center\nin a space designated L323 as per lease agreements between the venue\nand the shopping center and as specified on the venue's liquor\nlicense.\n\nThe venue is expected to hire 150 employees and contribute significant\nsales tax revenue.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  None.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: Increased tax revenue.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately.\n\n",
